# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 SpecSierra (atlantic-engine)
# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Patrick Quinn
# SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
#
# Header self-sufficiency / missing-include fixes for WTF and PAL.
# Merged from 12 patches: webkit-ramsize-cstddef, webkit-wtf-header-includes,
# webkit-wtf-platform-stdint, webkit-wtf-glib-platform,
# webkit-wtf-glib-header-includes, webkit-wtf-linux-header-includes,
# webkit-wtf-posix-unix-platform, webkit-memoryfootprint-cstddef,
# webkit-unistdextras-includes, webkit-pal-system-header-includes,
# webkit-pal-text-header-includes, webkit-pal-header-owners.
#
# All of it is one class of problem: a file uses size_t / uint8_t / <span> /
# ENABLE() / USE() / OS() / PLATFORM() / WTF_EXPORT_PRIVATE /
# WTF_MAKE_TZONE_ALLOCATED without including the header that owns it, and only
# the SFOS sysroot + this toolchain combination exposes it. Purely mechanical
# #include insertion — behaviour-neutral.
#
# MAINTENANCE: this whole class should stop being a patch. The intended
# replacement is a force-included prelude (-include cstdint/cstddef/span in
# CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS, plus a generated WTF prelude for targets that have the WTF
# include dirs) — see docs/STREAMLINE-PLAN.md A1. Until then, on a version bump
# regenerate rather than hand-fix: apply, build, and re-derive the insertions
# from the compile errors.
#
# Pacific (build/patches/atlantic/, replaces Atlantic's at a91f8ec for WPE
# WebKit 2.54.2): 2.54.1 renamed wtf/linux/RealTimeThreads.h to
# HighPriorityThreads.h (thread QOS by nice level and utilization clamp, with
# RealtimeKit only for the user-interactive threads). The same two includes
# go into the renamed header; nothing else changed.
#
# ---
